      "title": "HOW TO USE — SEED A/B + AUDIO REF",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# SEED SEARCH + OPTIONAL AUDIO REFERENCE\n\n**Seed A:** Main branch; choose randomize for seed search, fixed after selecting a winner.\n\n**Seed B:** All five B nodes are BYPASSED by default (mode 4). Select B sampler, both B decoders and B output; Ctrl+B to enable them for side-by-side generation. Both branches share the same model, prompt and references, but use independent seeds. B costs an additional sample pass.\n\n**Audio reference:** Load your example sound in the blue LoadAudio node. It starts BYPASSED. Select the node and press Ctrl+B to enable. Press Ctrl+B again to disable. It connects to optional ref_audios.ref_audio_0, and is NOT an audio replacement or a post-processing mix.\n\n**Important:** Use a valid audio file before enabling. Keep B bypassed to generate only A."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "# SEED SEARCH + OPTIONAL AUDIO REFERENCE\n\n**Seed A:** Main branch; choose randomize for seed search, fixed after selecting a winner.\n\n**Seed B:** All five B nodes are BYPASSED by default (mode 4). Select B sampler, both B decoders and B output; Ctrl+B to enable them for side-by-side generation. Both branches share the same model, prompt and references, but use independent seeds. B costs an additional sample pass.\n\n**Audio reference:** Load your example sound in the blue LoadAudio node. It starts BYPASSED. Select the node and press Ctrl+B to enable. Press Ctrl+B again to disable. It connects to optional ref_audios.ref_audio_0, and is NOT an audio replacement or a post-processing mix.\n\n**Important:** Use a valid audio file before enabling. Keep B bypassed to generate only A."
      },
